{
  "_comment": [
    "CellTypist label -> CL id, the one hand-made decision a standard-annotator baseline needs.",
    "basis = how the correspondence is justified:",
    "  name      the label names this CL term after normalisation (case, plural, punctuation only)",
    "  synonym   the label is a standard abbreviation / synonym of that CL term's name",
    "  coarsened the label denotes a subtype the register has no term for; mapped to the CL term it is a",
    "            subtype of. A coarsened prediction is never counted as an exact hit -- only as",
    "            hierarchy-consistent (see baselines/step5_score.py).",
    "Every cl_id below is checked against artifacts/v2/cl_terms.json before it is used; an unknown id is a",
    "hard error, not a silent skip. A label not listed here and not resolved mechanically is 'unmapped':",
    "the prediction cannot be expressed in the corpus's label space at all, and is reported as a rate.",
    "Source for the models' own label strings: baselines/out/celltypist_models.json (dumped from the model files)."
  ],
